23	 * {@code textures/entity/<model>/mask.png} (per pixel: which colour role it is, how much of the dark colour to mix in, a
24	 * highlight amount) and one {@code variants.json} of palettes; the first time a variant is drawn this paints it into a
25	 * {@link DynamicTexture} and caches it. So a dragon colour is one line of JSON, not one more PNG, and a monster may
26	 * even ask for a raw {@code "#RRGGBB"} variant that derives its palette from that colour.</p>
27	 *
28	 * <p>Mask encoding (RGBA, written by {@code tools/blockbench/mobs/mobkit.py}): R = mix toward {@code dark},
29	 * G = role * 40 (base, dark, belly, horn, membrane, eye), B = whiten, A = 255 painted / 0 empty.</p>
